SUMMARY:Community Photo event-Automotive building during CNE
DESCRIPTION:The Toronto Photography Group\nThe Grand Finale of Our Communi
 ty Photo Summer Camp Series Get ready for a very special photography exper
 ience as West Toronto Photography Group takes over one of Exhibition Place
 ’s most spectacular historic spaces for the finale of our 2026 Community
  Photo Summer Camp series!\n\n## Link for tickets -https://www.wtpg.ngo/ev
 ent-details/community-photo-summer-camp-finale-pwyc-workshop-at-automotive
 -building-during-cne\n\n## About the event\n\n# ART DECO\, LIGHT & FORM\n\
 n### The Grand Finale of Our Community Photo Summer Camp Series\n\nGet rea
 dy for a very special photography experience as **West Toronto Photography
  Group** takes over one of Exhibition Place’s most spectacular historic 
 spaces for the **finale of our 2026 Community Photo Summer Camp series!**\
 nFor this workshop\, we’re bringing together **architecture\, fashion\, 
 creative styling and professional studio lighting** inside the breathtakin
 g **Automotive Building at Exhibition Place**.\nBuilt in **1929**\, the Au
 tomotive Building is a remarkable piece of Toronto architectural history. 
 Designed by Toronto architect Douglas Kertland during the height of the Ar
 t Deco era\, its bold geometric forms\, elegant Beaux-Arts influences and 
 grand exhibition spaces were originally created to showcase the automobile
 . At its opening\, it was described as the largest structure in North Amer
 ica designed exclusively for displaying passenger vehicles.\nAnd now\, nea
 rly a century later\, we're going to put it to a very different use: **mak
 ing photographs.**\n\n![](https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1eaf19_60fb64
 d4e97f4bf48a6c1ce659c96f77~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_767\,h_528\,al_c\,lg_1\,q_85\
 ,enc_auto/1eaf19_60fb64d4e97f4bf48a6c1ce659c96f77~mv2.jpg)\n\n## ✨ LIGHT
 . FASHION. ARCHITECTURE.\n\nWe're bringing some serious lighting firepower
  to this workshop\, including **Elinchrom 5 flashes**\, giving participant
 s the opportunity to work with professional lighting equipment and explore
  how controlled light can transform both a subject and an architectural en
 vironment.\nAdding to the creative experience\, designer **Adrianna Fulop*
 * will be styling our model in a stunning custom look designed to compleme
 nt the character\, scale and drama of this incredible building.\nWe'll exp
 eriment with dramatic lighting\, directional light\, shadow\, shape and co
 mposition while using the Automotive Building's architecture as our enormo
 us studio.\nThink **Art Deco glamour meets contemporary fashion photograph
 y**.\nAnd because the **Canadian National Exhibition is happening at the s
 ame time**\, your workshop experience also includes access to the CNE afte
 r the evening workshop. That means you can make a full photographic advent
 ure out of the evening—exploring Exhibition Place\, photographing the CN
 E and taking advantage of all the visual possibilities surrounding the wor
 kshop after.\n![](https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1eaf19_7f326a11584843
 eb8ea1f9c84fabceea~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1125\,h_1421\,al_c\,q_85\,enc_auto/1e
 af19_7f326a11584843eb8ea1f9c84fabceea~mv2.jpg)\n\n## 📸 OUR COMMUNITY PH
 OTO SUMMER CAMP FINALE\n\nThis is the **LAST Community Photo Summer Camp e
 vent of the summer**—and we're going out with a bang!\nAs with our summe
 r series\, this is a **Pay What You Can community photography event**\, de
 signed to make professional photography education and creative opportuniti
 es accessible to as many photographers as possible.\nWe're limiting the wo
 rkshop to **just 12 photographers**.\nThat small-group format means more s
 hooting time\, more opportunities to work with the lighting setups\, more 
 questions answered and more individual attention from the instructor.\n![]
 (https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1eaf19_7080a31f2487473387e85dd221b9f87
 d~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1127\,h_1418\,al_c\,q_85\,enc_auto/1eaf19_7080a31f2487
 473387e85dd221b9f87d~mv2.jpg)\n\n### ONLY 12 SPOTS — PAY WHAT YOU CAN\n\
 nThere is **no fixed cost workshop fee**.\nChoose what you can afford to p
 ay and help us continue bringing accessible photography education and comm
 unity arts programming to Toronto. This workshop includes access to the CN
 E grounds in the evening after the workshop\n\n## THE WORKSHOP TEAM\n\n**I
 nstructor:** Phil Sutherland\n\n**Designer/Stylist:** Adrianna Fulop\n\n**
 Model:** To be announced\n\n**Assistant:** Volunteer to be announced\n\n##
  WHAT YOU'LL EXPLORE\n\nThis is an intermediate-level lighting workshop fo
 cused on creating strong\, intentional photographs using the relationship 
 between **light\, shadow\, fashion\, architecture and form**.\nWe'll explo
 re:\n\n* Professional Elinchrom flash techniques\n* Lighting large archite
 ctural spaces\n* Working with directional and dramatic light\n* Balancing 
 ambient light with flash\n* Creating shape and dimension with light\n* Usi
 ng architecture as a compositional element\n* Fashion and editorial-style 
 photography\n* Working collaboratively with a model and stylist\n* Develop
 ing creative lighting setups rather than simply copying a formula\n* Makin
 g the most of a challenging and visually spectacular location\n\nMost impo
 rtantly\, **you'll be shooting**. This isn't a workshop where you spend th
 ree hours watching someone else make photographs.\n\n## THE AUTOMOTIVE BUI
 LDING\n\nThe Automotive Building is one of the hidden architectural gems o
 f Exhibition Place.\nOpened in 1929 during Toronto's fascination with the 
 automobile\, the building originally housed the CNE's National Motor Show.
  During the Second World War it was even used by the Royal Canadian Navy a
 s **HMCS York**.\nToday\, its dramatic interior\, monumental scale and dis
 tinctive period architecture make it an extraordinary location for photogr
 aphy.\nWe're incredibly excited to have the opportunity to bring our commu
 nity into this historic space and see what we can create together.\n\n## W
 HAT TO BRING\n\nPlease bring:\n\n* DSLR\, mirrorless or medium-format came
 ra\n* Your preferred lenses\n* Fully charged batteries\n* Freshly formatte
 d memory card(s)\n* A general-purpose lens\n* Pen and paper if you'd like 
 to take notes\n\n**Tripods and camera supports are not required.**\n\n### 
 WIRELESS TRIGGERS\n\nWe provide wireless triggers for most mainstream came
 ra systems. If you're unsure whether your camera is compatible\, contact u
 s before the workshop and we'll be happy to confirm.\n\n## MODEL RELEASE\n
 \nA **West Toronto Photography Group model release** will be provided to e
 ach participant.\nThe release covers non-commercial photography and images
  created for educational and training purposes. The model will sign the re
 leases\, and printed copies will be provided to participating photographer
 s.\n\n## ABOUT WEST TORONTO PHOTOGRAPHY GROUP\n\n**West Toronto Photograph
 y Group is an Indigenous-run\, not-for-profit arts organization** dedicate
 d to supporting photographers\, sharing knowledge and making photography a
 nd arts programming accessible to the community.\nOur workshops are about 
 more than learning technical skills. They're about **meeting other photogr
 aphers\, experimenting\, building confidence\, creating new work and havin
 g a great time making photographs together.**\n\n## ONE LAST SUMMER SHOOT.
  ONE AMAZING LOCATION.\n\nWe've spent the summer photographing\, learning 
 and exploring Toronto together.\nNow we're bringing the series to one of E
 xhibition Place's most spectacular historic buildings for a finale that co
 mbines **Art Deco architecture\, fashion\, professional lighting and the e
 nergy of the CNE.**\n**Only 12 spots. Pay What You Can. Professional Elinc
 hrom lighting. An incredible designer. A stunning location. And one last c
 hance to make photographs with the WTPG community this summer.**\n**Come j
 oin us for the finale. Let's make some magic with light.**\n\nThank you to
  Exhibition Place for access to this amazing building\, Thank you to CNE f
 or the passes and Elinchrom for the amazing flash gear. Once signed up and
  confirmed we will email everyone with specific instructions on entry poin
 t and location details\, but we will be meeting in an easy to meet point a
 t the Princes gate at 5:30
