SUMMARY:Art and Form intermediate lighting workshop w Ciara
DESCRIPTION:The Toronto Photography Group\n## LINK to purchase tickets for
  event- [https://www.wtpg.ngo/event-details/wtpg-signature-series-art-and-
 form-intermediate-level-lighting-with-ciara](https://www.wtpg.ngo/event-de
 tails/wtpg-signature-series-art-and-form-intermediate-level-lighting-with-
 ciara)\n\n## About the event\n\n# Light\, Art & Form — Intermediate Art 
 Nude Photography Workshop\n\n![](https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1eaf19
 _36e8e2cfab3e43db8b02a308cfd28143~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1686\,h_844\,al_c\,q_8
 5\,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01\,enc_auto/1eaf19_36e8e2cfab3e43db8b02a308cfd28143~mv
 2.jpg)\n\n## About the Event\n\n**10:00 AM – 12:00 PM**\nWe are excited 
 to present **Light\, Art & Form**\, an intermediate-level studio photograp
 hy workshop exploring the creative possibilities of **art nude photography
 \, light and form**\, featuring the talented model **Ciara Antoski**.\nThi
 s hands-on workshop is designed for photographers who want to develop thei
 r understanding of studio lighting while creating dramatic\, artistic and 
 carefully composed images for their portfolios.\nWorking in a small\, inti
 mate group\, we'll explore several professional lighting setups and discus
 s how the **position\, direction\, quality and shape of light** can transf
 orm the appearance of the human form.\n![](https://static.wixstatic.com/me
 dia/1eaf19_1102af7eb2474a63bc94b3ad85ccabcb~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1686\,h_844\
 ,al_c\,q_85\,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01\,enc_auto/1eaf19_1102af7eb2474a63bc94b3ad8
 5ccabcb~mv2.jpg)\n\n## Workshop Details\n\nAre you passionate about art nu
 de photography? Do you want to better understand how professional photogra
 phers create dramatic and beautiful lighting?\nThis workshop is focused on
  **learning through doing**. Phil Sutherland will guide participants throu
 gh each setup\, explaining the lighting choices\, modifiers\, angles and t
 echniques used to create the desired look.\nParticipants will have opportu
 nities to photograph each setup while receiving guidance and feedback thro
 ughout the session.\n![](https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1eaf19_13ca992
 b3f9e4f2faccb98a3ecc45847~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_918\,h_613\,al_c\,q_85\,enc_au
 to/1eaf19_13ca992b3f9e4f2faccb98a3ecc45847~mv2.jpg)\n\n### Framing & Compo
 sition\n\nDuring the workshop\, we'll explore several approaches to photog
 raphing the figure\, including:\n\n* **2/3-body compositions**\n* **Floor-
 level compositions featuring lingerie**\n* **Full-body compositions**\n* E
 xploring how framing\, negative space and perspective affect the final ima
 ge\n* Using light and shadow to emphasize form and create mood\n\n## Works
 hop Team\n\n**Instructor:** Phil Sutherland\n\n**Model:** Ciara Antoski\n\
 n**Assistant:** Volunteer to be announced\nCiara brings considerable exper
 ience and professionalism to the workshop\, and we're thrilled to have her
  working with us for this session.\n\n### Small Group — Maximum 6 Photog
 raphers\n\nTo provide a better learning and shooting experience\, we are l
 imiting this workshop to **a maximum of six participants**.\nKeeping the g
 roup small allows for more individual attention\, more opportunities to as
 k questions and meaningful shooting time with each lighting setup.\n\n## A
 bout West Toronto Photography Group\n\nAs an **Indigenous-run\, not-for-pr
 ofit arts organization**\, West Toronto Photography Group is committed to 
 supporting photographers\, sharing knowledge and making arts programming a
 ccessible to the community.\nOur workshops are designed to create a welcom
 ing and professional environment where photographers can learn\, experimen
 t\, meet other artists and—most importantly—have fun making photograph
 s.\n\n## Workshop Information\n\n**Maximum Participants:** 6\n\n**Workshop
  Fee:** CAD $125 + HST and applicable vendor fee\n\n## What Should I Bring
 ?\n\nPlease bring:\n\n* DSLR\, mirrorless or medium-format camera\n* Your 
 preferred lenses\n* Fully charged batteries\n* Freshly formatted memory ca
 rd(s)\n* A general-purpose lens\n* Pen and paper if you'd like to take not
 es\n\n**Tripods and camera supports are not required** for this workshop.\
 n\n### Wireless Triggers\n\nWe provide wireless triggers for most mainstre
 am camera systems. If you're unsure whether your camera is compatible\, pl
 ease contact us before the workshop and we'll be happy to confirm.\n\n## M
 odel Release\n\nA **West Toronto Photography Group model release** will be
  provided to each participant.\nThe release covers **non-commercial use an
 d photography created for educational and training purposes**. The model w
 ill sign the releases\, and printed copies will be provided to participati
 ng photographers.\n\n## Cancellation & Transfer Policy\n\nIf we\, as organ
 izers\, need to postpone or cancel the workshop\, refunds will be issued w
 ithin **72 hours**.\nWe understand that sometimes circumstances prevent pa
 rticipants from attending. If you can no longer attend\, please contact us
  as soon as possible. We will do our best to help you **resell your worksh
 op spot to another member of the group**.\nIf we are able to resell your s
 pot\, you will be reimbursed for the ticket price. If the spot cannot be r
 esold\, you may transfer your registration to another person to attend in 
 your place\; unfortunately\, **no refund will be available if the spot rem
 ains unsold**.\n\n## Join Us\n\nCome explore the relationship between **li
 ght\, shadow and the human form** in this focused intermediate photography
  workshop.\nWhether you're looking to strengthen your studio lighting skil
 ls\, expand your portfolio or explore new approaches to art nude photograp
 hy\, **Light\, Art & Form** offers an opportunity to learn\, experiment an
 d create in a supportive professional environment.\nWe look forward to wel
 coming you to the studio!
