SUMMARY:Pin Up Perfection w Ciara
DESCRIPTION:The Toronto Photography Group\n## Details\n\n\\#\\# Details\nL
 ink for tickets - [https://www.wtpg.ngo/event-details/pin-up-perfection-ph
 otography-lighting-workshop-2](https://www.wtpg.ngo/event-details/pin-up-p
 erfection-photography-lighting-workshop-2)\n\\#\\# About the event\n**Quic
 k Details**\n1:00 pm - 3:00 pm Pin Up Perfection! Photography lighting wor
 kshop\nModel Ciara Antoski\nInstructor: Phil Sutherland\nAssistant/ Volunt
 eer to be announced soon\,\n\\# Pin Up Perfection\\! — Photography Light
 ing Workshop\n\\#\\# Quick Details\n**1:00 PM – 3:00 PM**\n**Pin Up Perf
 ection! — Photography Lighting Workshop**\n**Model:** Ciara Antoski\n**I
 nstructor:** Phil Sutherland\n**Assistant/Volunteer:** To be announced\nSt
 ep back into the golden age of **retro Pin Up photography** for a fun\, ha
 nds-on studio lighting workshop designed to help you build your confidence
 \, understand studio lighting and create great images.\nExpect **oldies tu
 nes\, vintage-inspired outfits\, classic Pin Up poses and some seriously f
 un lighting!** We are thrilled to have **Ciara Antoski** joining us as our
  model. Ciara is an amazing model\, and we are very lucky to have her help
 ing us bring this workshop to life.\n\n* \\!\\[img\\]\\(\\)\n* \\!\\[img\\
 ]\\(\\)\n* \\!\\[img\\]\\(\\)\n\n\\#\\#\\# What You'll Learn\nWhether Pin 
 Up photography is a new interest or an established passion\, this workshop
  will help you take your studio lighting skills to the next level.\nThis *
 *two-hour\, information-packed workshop** is limited to **only 6 photograp
 hers**\, giving everyone plenty of opportunity to ask questions\, experime
 nt with the lighting and get hands-on shooting time.\nDuring the workshop\
 , we will:\n**1\\. Explore the equipment**\nGet a detailed introduction to
  the studio equipment\, modifiers and lighting tools we will be using. We 
 will build and adjust **three different lighting setups** throughout the w
 orkshop.\n**2\\. Discover the Old\\-School Pin Up Look**\nWe'll explore th
 e history and techniques behind classic Pin Up photography\, including how
  older studio spaces\, lights and modifiers were used to create that disti
 nctive vintage look. We'll also compare traditional techniques with modern
  studio lighting tools.\n**3\\. Shoot Three Lighting Setups**\nWe will cre
 ate and photograph **three different lighting setups**\, giving each parti
 cipant opportunities to shoot\, experiment and see firsthand how changing 
 the position\, size and direction of the light affects the final image.\n\
 \#\\# Who Is This Workshop For?\nThis workshop is suitable for **photograp
 hers of all skill levels** who want to learn more about studio photography
  and become more comfortable working with professional lighting equipment.
 \nYou don't need to be an experienced studio photographer. We'll demonstra
 te the lighting techniques\, explain the equipment and give everyone oppor
 tunities to photograph each setup.\nWe'll also discuss how different modif
 iers—including **reflectors\, umbrellas\, softboxes\, grids\, snoots and
  beauty dishes**—can be used to shape and control light.\n\\#\\#\\# Maxi
 mum 6 Participants\nKeeping the group small means **more shooting time\, m
 ore opportunities to ask questions and more hands-on learning** for everyo
 ne.\nTime is valuable\, so we keep our workshops efficient\, practical and
  focused on getting you behind the camera. You'll spend less time standing
  around and more time **learning\, shooting and experimenting with light.*
 *\n\\#\\# What We Provide\n📸 A professional and comfortable studio envi
 ronment\n💡 A variety of professional lighting equipment and modifiers\n
 🎯 Hands-on instruction and lighting demonstrations\n👩 A professional
  model with multiple shooting opportunities\n🤝 Time to network and lear
 n with other photographers\n📚 Practical instruction you can take back t
 o your own studio or shoots\n**No turkey shoots!** Everyone gets opportuni
 ties to photograph the model and work with the lighting setups.\n\\#\\# Wh
 at Should I Bring?\n**Your camera!** Any DSLR or mirrorless camera with ma
 nual controls will work perfectly.\nPlease bring:\n\n* A camera capable of
  manual exposure\n* Freshly charged batteries\n* Formatted memory cards\n*
  Your favourite lens — anything from approximately **10mm–160mm** can 
 work\, depending on your camera and shooting style\n* Your curiosity and p
 assion for photography!\n\nDon't worry if you're not sure what settings to
  use. **We'll help you get started with the appropriate exposure settings 
 and explain why we're using them.**\nMost importantly\, bring your enthusi
 asm and a willingness to learn. **We'll bring the fun!**\n\\#\\# Who Shoul
 d Take Our Workshops?\nOur workshops are perfect for photographers who hav
 e a **basic understanding of their camera and manual settings**\, but they
  are also welcoming to photographers at more advanced levels who want to e
 xplore new lighting techniques.\nWhether you're:\n\n* Just starting to sho
 ot in a studio\n* Looking to understand studio lighting better\n* Interest
 ed in Pin Up and vintage photography\n* Wanting to experiment with profess
 ional modifiers\n* Looking for new lighting ideas for your own photography
 \n* Or simply want to spend two hours making great photographs with other 
 photographers\n\n**Pin Up Perfection! is designed to be fun\, practical an
 d packed with information.**\nCome learn the lighting\, photograph an amaz
 ing model\, experiment with classic Pin Up techniques and leave with new s
 kills you can put to work in your own photography.\nIf Pin up photography 
 lighting is one of your interest or your passion and you want to upgrade y
 our studio lighting skills\nYou will be substantially informed from this w
 ell paced 1.5 hour group workshop and we are limiting the workshop size to
  only 6 people to allow more time for questions and learning.\n1 - This wo
 rkshop will spend the two hours going through a detailed run down of equip
 ment names and how we will use them as we set up the lighting for each of 
 the 3x setups we will build during the workshop.\n2 - We will discuss old 
 school Pin Up shooting and how the older modifiers and studio spaces worke
 d and take time to introduce different tools used to create images in stud
 io that are old and new school\n3 - We will shoot 3 different lighting set
  ups in the 2 hour lighting workshop and have a great time in studio.\n\n*
  \\!\\[img\\]\\(\\)\n* \\!\\[img\\]\\(\\)\n* \\!\\[img\\]\\(\\)
